WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.739 --> 00:00:02.300
The Marvels have landed.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:07.041
The first teaser for the newest MCU adventure,
which brings together Carol Danvers, Monica

00:00:07.041 --> 00:00:12.500
Rambeau, and Kamala Khan, is packed with treats
for fans with keen eyes.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.850
The internet at large's fascination with cat
videos is proof that a cute feline is often

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.789
a welcome addition to anything.

00:00:19.789 --> 00:00:24.380
Make the cat an eldritch tentacle abomination,
and suddenly, one has the fearsome creature

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:26.110
known as a Flerken.

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:30.849
Though these beings appear to be simple house
cats, Flerkens are actually incredibly intelligent

00:00:30.849 --> 00:00:35.220
and contain pocket dimensions that allow them
to hide their deadly tentacles.

00:00:35.692 --> 00:00:36.590
"The cat?"

00:00:36.753 --> 00:00:38.509
"This isn't what you're afraid of, is it?"

00:00:38.509 --> 00:00:39.645
"That's not a cat."

00:00:39.754 --> 00:00:44.730
The species was originally introduced to the
MCU in "Captain Marvel" by way of Goose, whom

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.090
nobody initially realizes is an alien.

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:50.149
But it soon becomes apparent how dangerous
these creatures are.

00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:54.680
In the teaser trailer for "The Marvels," Kamala
is quickly introduced to Goose's true nature,

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:55.930
much to her horror.

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:59.680
For fans of "Captain Marvel," it's great to
see Goose back in action, but it also appears

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.300
that there might be an entire litter of Flerken
kittens running about, which is an adorable

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.790
yet terrifying prospect for any foe.

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:10.790
It will be fascinating how these deceptive
and cunning creatures fit into the movie's

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:11.790
greater plot.

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:17.710
From Mar-Vell's laboratory to the Kyln, the
MCU's characters love to visit space-based

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.689
facilities whenever the opportunity presents
itself.

00:01:20.689 --> 00:01:24.439
And with "The Marvels" set to explore the
cosmos, the franchise is adding a space station

00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:25.439
to the mix.

00:01:25.439 --> 00:01:29.659
The opening moments of the "Marvels" teaser
trailer take place on the SABER Space Station,

00:01:29.659 --> 00:01:34.590
which looks a whole lot like the comics headquarters
of SWORD, the Sentient World Observation and

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.860
Response Department, SHIELD's space-based
counterpart.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:42.869
In the MCU, Monica Rambeau's mother, Maria,
founded SWORD, and Monica served as a SWORD

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.409
agent in "WandaVision."

00:01:44.409 --> 00:01:49.579
The MCU acronym is slightly different from
the comics, with the "W" standing for "Weapon."

00:01:49.579 --> 00:01:54.369
With the Skrulls set to play a major role
in the future of the MCU, it's entirely possible

00:01:54.369 --> 00:01:58.370
that the SABER Space Station will be used
to explore their corner of the galaxy.

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:02.116
For now, the station's purpose is unknown,
although Kamala does wonder…

00:02:02.297 --> 00:02:03.847
"Is this an Avengers test?"

00:02:04.488 --> 00:02:07.920
Although one might assume that "The Marvels"
will showcase three different variations of

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:13.433
the same powers, each character has a unique
set of skills that are born from their specific origins.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:18.550
Carol gains hers from exposure to an experimental
energy source, Kamala gets hers from a bangle

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:23.040
in combination with her alien heritage, and
Monica's powers come from repeated forays

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:27.790
across Wanda Maximoff's energy barrier around
Westview in "WandaVision."

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:32.684
Kamala can create hard light constructs and
Carol can harness a powerful galactic power source.

00:02:32.684 --> 00:02:37.440
Monica, meanwhile, explains that she can manipulate
light energy, which allows her to project

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.260
energy blasts as well as become intangible.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:44.420
Considering her comic book counterpart, who
is sometimes called Photon, is able to control

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:49.260
energy on the entire electromagnetic spectrum,
Monica stands to develop even more powers

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:50.900
over the course of "The Marvels."

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.459
Either way, she's sure to be a powerful hero.

00:02:54.638 --> 00:02:58.360
Making use of alien technology is a recurring
trend for SHIELD.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:02.560
From the very first "Avengers" movie, it becomes
apparent that Earth is hopelessly outgunned

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:05.330
and outmatched on an intergalactic scale.

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:10.080
So Nick Fury has no qualms with scavenging
weapons research from HYDRA or experimenting

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.370
on the Tesseract to develop a powerful new
energy source that would better defend Earth

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:17.120
from alien invasions and interdimensional
warlords.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:21.379
At the beginning of the teaser trailer for
"The Marvels," Monica reports on her proximity

00:03:21.379 --> 00:03:26.550
to the perimeter of a Jump Point, which shows
that Earth is experimenting with jump technology.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:31.080
This type of technology is featured predominantly
in the "Guardians of the Galaxy" franchise,

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:35.519
and it is the means by which space-faring
beings travel quickly across the universe.

00:03:35.519 --> 00:03:39.280
Although the Jump Point shown in the teaser
trailer doesn't seem to be nearly as refined

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:43.970
or advanced as the Universal Neural Teleportation
Network depicted in "Guardians," its mere

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:47.970
appearance implies that Earth is quickly catching
up to the rest of the universe.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:51.840
Considering the sheer number of aliens who
have interacted with Earth over the past decade

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:56.269
or so, it makes perfect sense as to why SHIELD
and Fury would want to learn as much as they

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:58.310
can as quickly as they can.

00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:02.950
Whether or not Earth develops this technology
independent of outside influence is anybody's

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:06.259
guess, but it is reassuring that humanity
is rapidly advancing.

00:04:07.712 --> 00:04:10.720
2023 is looking to be a big year for Nick
Fury.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:14.990
The superspy and former Director of SHIELD
seems to be getting cozy up in space, but

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:19.160
his eye patch may signal when "The Marvels"
takes place in the MCU timeline.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:24.100
In late March 2023, Vanity Fair dropped a
piece on "Secret Invasion" in which Jackson

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:28.960
said his character sheds the iconic eye patch
in the Disney+ series as part of his character

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:32.330
development, making it seem like the accessory
will become a relic of the past.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:36.600
However, in "The Marvels" teaser trailer,
Fury is still wearing his eye patch, meaning

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:40.570
that the sequel almost certainly takes place
before the events of "Secret Invasion" in

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:42.240
the MCU timeline.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:46.410
Marvel Studios' most recent release, "Ant-Man
and the Wasp: Quantumania," is the latest

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:51.191
event in the MCU timeline, with "Black Panther:
Wakanda Forever" before it and "Thor: Love

00:04:51.191 --> 00:04:53.350
and Thunder" in the timeline before that.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:57.759
Presumably, "The Marvels" will take Ant-Man's
place as the most recent MCU entry, though

00:04:57.759 --> 00:05:03.397
it does also seem to take place at least partially
immediately after the "Ms. Marvel" Disney+ series.

00:05:03.397 --> 00:05:07.160
It seems like Marvel planned for "The Marvels"
to come out before "Secret Invasion," or at

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.831
least at roughly the same time.

00:05:08.831 --> 00:05:09.981
But that's not the case.

00:05:09.981 --> 00:05:15.289
"Secret Invasion" debuts June 21, while "Marvels"
is slated for November 10, after being pushed

00:05:15.289 --> 00:05:16.960
back from a July release.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:21.030
That said, neither story is likely to suffer
because of the shakeup in the release schedule.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:25.120
But it will be interesting to see a grizzled
Nick Fury taking on the Skrulls before teaming

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:28.080
up with the light-hearted Kamala Khan in "The
Marvels."

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:33.150
That's assuming Nick Fury in the trailer actually
is the real Nick Fury, and not a Skrull, like

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:34.710
in "Spider-Man: Far From Home."

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:37.030
When it comes to Fury, all bets are off.

00:05:38.158 --> 00:05:42.430
One of the mechanisms that brings the heroes
together in "The Marvels" is a mysterious

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:47.160
process that causes Ms. Marvel, Monica, and
Captain Marvel to switch places whenever one

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:48.460
of them powers up.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:52.754
At one point, Monica explains that their powers
are somehow intrinsically connected.

00:05:52.754 --> 00:05:55.387
"OK, so, our powers are entangled."

00:05:55.387 --> 00:06:00.200
This place-swapping team-up was teased long
ago at the very end of the "Ms. Marvel" Disney+

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:05.220
series, which features an incredibly confused
Carol Danvers manifesting in the Khan household,

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:09.569
being launched into Kamala's closet and finding
herself surrounded by Captain Marvel merchandise.

00:06:09.569 --> 00:06:13.630
Now, it's clear that the scene also appears
in "The Marvels," and it's expanded upon in

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:17.290
the teaser trailer, as the experienced hero
tries to take in the fact that she's gone

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:21.090
from battling alien forces to standing in
a nerdy teenager's room.

00:06:22.406 --> 00:06:27.390
Kamala Khan changed the game when she was
first introduced to Marvel Comics in 2013.

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:31.620
She's the first Muslim superhero to ever headline
her own comic book series, as well as the

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:35.190
first Muslim character to spearhead a live-action
Marvel property.

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:40.410
She's been a fresh addition to the MCU, especially
in regard to diversifying its roster of superheroes.

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:45.190
The Disney+ series "Ms. Marvel" received heaps
of praise for these elements, and it seems

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:48.790
that "The Marvels" will continue to honor
the character's cultural heritage.

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:53.090
The teaser trailer for the upcoming blockbuster
includes some scenes in which Nick Fury and

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:57.340
Monica Rambeau visit Kamala's family and explain
how their powers are entangled with those

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:58.500
of their daughter.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:02.310
The footage makes it clear that the Khan family
will play a key part in the movie, suggesting

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:06.090
that the franchise will continue to illustrate
the importance of her cultural background

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:09.240
and how it influences her as a superhero as
she matures.

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:15.130
When news broke of Zawe Ashton joining "The
Marvels," Marvel Studios shrouded her role

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:19.150
in their typical secrecy, only revealing that
she's playing the movie's villain.

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:23.060
A press release from Marvel accompanying the
teaser trailer confirmed that her character

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:28.590
is an all-but-unknown one from the comics:
a gender-swapped version of the Kree General

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:29.590
Dar-Benn.

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:33.570
In the teaser trailer, we see her surrounded
by an army of Kree soldiers, carrying a staff

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:38.310
oddly reminiscent of Ronan the Accuser's weapon
in "Guardians of the Galaxy" — more on that

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:41.560
in a bit! — and with a female Accuser trailing
her.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:46.050
If Dar-Benn's name doesn't immediately ring
a bell, that's to be expected, as the general

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:49.440
is a relatively obscure character from Marvel
Comics.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:53.400
There's not much to know about Dar-Benn other
than he's a general who became an emperor

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:54.970
for the Kree Empire.

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:58.620
The villain seems like the perfect sort of
obscure character for the studio to bring

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:03.620
into the MCU, since there's lots of room for
reimagining Dar-Benn to suit the needs of

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:04.620
the story.

00:08:05.789 --> 00:08:09.949
Speaking of characters carrying interesting
staffs, the teaser trailer for "The Marvels"

00:08:09.949 --> 00:08:14.669
shows Carol Danvers getting a weapon of her
own, when we see our titular superhero group

00:08:14.669 --> 00:08:19.039
facing off against an antagonist who appears
to be Zawe Ashton's Dar-Benn.

00:08:19.039 --> 00:08:23.930
Captain Marvel, Spectrum, and Ms. Marvel all
sport brand-new costumes, but we can't help

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:26.530
but notice that Carol's holding a staff behind
her back.

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:30.090
Pair that with the shot of her swinging at
the villain with a hammer-like staff a few

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:34.380
seconds later, and it all but confirms Captain
Marvel will wield a weapon in the movie's

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:35.690
climactic fight.

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:40.050
This weapon looks a lot like a Kree Cosmi-Rod,
the weapon of choice for the Accusers.

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:44.560
MCU fans saw Ronan wield one in "Guardians
of the Galaxy," and the trailer also shows

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:48.960
Ashton's villain carrying her own Cosmi-Rod,
if it isn't the same one.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:53.710
While Captain Marvel is generally known more
for energy blasts than melee attacks, we can't

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:58.470
wait to see what one of the MCU's strongest
heroes is capable of with such a powerful

00:08:58.470 --> 00:08:59.850
weapon in hand.

